.TH PICK 1
.SH NAME
pick \- picking without a hit test
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/pick
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Pick
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Graphics/Pick.HC
demonstration.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
A hundred and twenty-eight apples.  The neat idea is that picking needs
no geometry: the device context is told to measure, for everything drawn
through it, the squared distance from the cursor to the nearest pixel
actually painted, so drawing the sprites is the pick.  The distance stays
squared throughout because, as the original notes, a square root is
expensive and the comparison does not need one.
.PP
The left button grabs the nearest apple and drags it, keeping the offset
from where it was grabbed.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "any key"
.TP
.B LMB
Drag the nearest apple
.TP
.B "any key"
Exit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/pick.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR draw3d (2),
.IR wm (1)
